    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe acceptance test creates an owner and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `$.displayName` to equal `\"LastName, FirstName\"`. I made the response DTO carry that computed field:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `displayName` read-only string property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field (and it's documented in the API).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a small `displayName(Owner)` helper (`lastName + \", \" + firstName`) and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression.\n\nPutting the formatting in the mapper keeps it in the single place responsible for `Owner \u2192 OwnerDto` translation, so every read path (create, get, list) returns `displayName` consistently, with no duplication and no new logic bolted onto the entity or the OfficeFloor functions. `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test passing.",
